From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emily Marx <emilykmarx@alumni.stanford.edu>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:30:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Expose the fake-webservers through Caddy's ingress

From Jamie Anzai-Wurfbain's 0e97cf9: an Ingress routes /fake-webserver to the
fake-webserver service's first port, so a client outside the cluster can reach
them at http://<node IP>:<Caddy's NodePort>/fake-webserver/metrics (paramtrack's
testbed queries them there). With the PR's namespace templated rather than
prombench-16075, and Caddy's rewrite-strip-prefix, since the fake-webservers
serve /metrics, not /fake-webserver/metrics.
---
 .../prombench/benchmark/4_fake-webserver.yaml | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/prombench/manifests/prombench/benchmark/4_fake-webserver.yaml b/prombench/manifests/prombench/benchmark/4_fake-webserver.yaml
index 21d3740..4094138 100644
--- a/prombench/manifests/prombench/benchmark/4_fake-webserver.yaml
+++ b/prombench/manifests/prombench/benchmark/4_fake-webserver.yaml
@@ -120,3 +120,24 @@ spec:
     targetPort: metrics5
   selector:
     app: fake-webserver
+---
+apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
+kind: Ingress
+metadata:
+  name: ingress-fake-webserver
+  namespace: prombench-{{ .PR_NUMBER }}
+  annotations:
+    caddy.ingress.kubernetes.io/disable-ssl-redirect: "true"
+    caddy.ingress.kubernetes.io/rewrite-strip-prefix: /fake-webserver
+spec:
+  ingressClassName: caddy
+  rules:
+  - http:
+      paths:
+      - path: /fake-webserver
+        pathType: Prefix
+        backend:
+          service:
+            name: fake-webserver
+            port:
+              number: 8080
-- 
